Transformer worth tens of millions of kroons on fire in the Louny region
In the morning, a fire engulfed a processor from the zeps company of the distribution centre near the municipality of Vokov na Lounsku.
According to Luka Marvan, a spokesman for the Firefighters of Osto, there are six units operating on the fire.
They were originally expected to let the processor oxidize, but they reviewed their opinion and extinguished the fire with a mixture of water, moss and a special substance.
The cause is a technical defect, an internal short-circuit of the transformer.
No one has been injured, and according to company spokeswoman Pavla Mandotova the incident does not endanger the secure operation of the transmission package.
The damage is estimated at a few tens of MK kroons, the exact figure can be known once the fire is extinguished.
According to Mandetova, the destroyed processor will have to be replaced by a new one.
She added that, in ten years of operation, there was nothing similar in the company and that such incidents were isolated.
The supply of electric power has not been halted, says the spokeswoman for Northern Bohemia Soia Holingerova Hendrychova, the functioning of households, administrations and industries has not been influenced by the burning of the Transformation Station.
It is the exclusive operator in the Czech territory of 400 kV and 220 kV transmission sets and power lines.
It maintains, renovates and develops 39 distribution substations with 67 transformers transferring electrical energy from transport packages to distribution assemblies and line layouts with a length of 4,339 kilometers.
Janura to file a libel complaint against three prefaults of SSD
Student Agency's owner Radim Janaura will today file a lawsuit for slewing against three social democrat prefaults.
And in concrete terms against Michal Haiek in the South Moravian region, against Radko Martunka in the Pardubice region and against the prefect of the Olomouc region Martin Tesaik.
Janura pointed this out in Dvacet minut de Radiournol.
The complaint is related to the company's attempt to exploit regional railways in certain regions.
