All three have attacked us and claim that the fine mouths are made, whereas we only made an offer for what they wanted themselves.
They claim that we are more expensive than the Czech Railways which isn't true because we know the prices of the Czech Railways that were signed last week.
So all we have to do is to defend ourselves.
In exchange for slander of the Student Agency, Janaura told Radiourn.
It also indicated that it had evidence that no region had proceeding in accordance with European law.
We are preparing a complaint to the European Commission for this.
Haiek considers that the filing of a complaint by Mr Janaura represents the continuation of his media show which serves as free publicity for his company and for his person.
Of course, I am prepared to defend my name and the name of my region and I call on the other prefets to do the same.
I assume that this will be an opportunity to make it clear that it is precisely Mr Janura who is manipulating public opinion and resorting to falsious arguments about regional rail transport.
Janura has already informed last week that it will invest some million kroons in an advertisement which will mention the unfavourable steps taken by the regions.
He has told Radiournal that he will interrupt the campaign after Christmas and intends to resume it after the New Year.
He pointed out that the campaign would target corruption in the broadest sense.
Janura began his campaign after the regions agreed to entrust the Czech Railways with the operation of the rail links for an order of approximately DKK 150 billion, without issuing a call for tenders.
According to Janaura, such a course of action is illegal and contrary to the position of the European Court of Justice.
