The only threat has been that if you didn't stop, we could lose our bus licenses.
He presented himself as a Member of the SSD, I don't know who it is, but I won't say his name, Janaura said today to Radiourn.
Pneumococcal vaccination will be free and optional
Pneumococcal vaccination will overwhelm old habits as early as January.
It will be the first to be gratuitous, at the same time optional for families.
There are already opinions that compulsory vaccination would be more effective.
Preparations for the introduction of free pneumococcal vaccination are plentiful.
The pharmaceutical institute already defines for vaccines the maximum prices that health insurance will pay.
Specialists are also clear in the vaccination process.
A new vaccination.
Possibilities for children in August.
Since January, children born last year as from 2 Aug can be vaccinated against pneumococci free of charge.
The condition is that they have not yet been vaccinated.
If we started vaccination last year or sooner, you will have to pay for the next vaccinations yourself.
The first dose of vaccine should be given between the child's 3rd and 5th Month.
Over the past last year, a quarter of their families voluntarily immunized their children against pneumococci.
Yet the parents were paying 1,600 kroons or more for a dose.
Princiation of the youngest requires four doses.
Specialists estimate that every year health insurance spends P.6 300 to 450,000 in vaccine doses.
However, there is a saving for medical care that unvaccinated children would require.
So far, the State has spent about 500,000 kroons a year on all child immunization.
Reimbursed vaccination has been introduced with the "Jaota package".
Pnemococci are the cause of inflammation of the middle ear but also serious infections including inflammation of the meninges and blood poisoning.
According to hospital investigations, there are up to 28 deaths of children under the age of 10 caused by pneumococcal infections.
Apart from the Czech Republic, about 40 other countries have introduced reimbursable vaccination.
Will vaccination be compulsory?
There are views on a possible vaccination obligation in the future.
Beginning in January, it must be regulated by insurance and optional.
For example, Nahlas Association President Rudolf Kalovska indicated that compulsory vaccination would be more positive.
Its association has for a long time promoted pneumococcal vaccination.
At an international conference in which our association participated, the specialists were not really satisfied with the fact that we have an optional vaccination.
It's not ideal.
On the other hand, we are pleased to have been able to impose at least this.
I believe that this is a direction that must now be followed, said Kalovsky.
But the Ministry of Health doesn’t want to change pneumococcal vaccination.
'We are completely not contemplating it at the moment,' his spokeswoman Vlastimil Sr'e.
Oppositary vaccination has its inconvenience, doctors say.
The President of the Specialized Society of Pediatricians, Hana Cabrnochova, acknowledges that vaccination based on volunteerism has its flaws.
If all the children were immunized, we could envisage a decrease in the renewals of vaccinations "In the situation in which the vaccine costs such a sum, I understand the decision making vaccination optional", says Cabrnochova.
Specialists expect more than 80 per cent of new parents to vaccinate their infants as early as next year.
Pneumococcal vaccination also marks the fact that it is the first vaccination of children that is financed by insurance rather than the State.
Cabrnochova explained that assurances would have to free up funds for prevention, thus saving on possible future medical care.
Physicians will have to buy their products themselves
However, this is related to the concerns of paediatric practitioners, which relate to the purchase of vaccines.
The original intention was to have the vaccines purchased through insurance, with doctors receiving them in the same way as other vaccine products supplied by the State.
Some MEPs feared, however, that this would allow insurance to 'deduce health insurance money'.
In this way, the doctors will have to buy the products and wait for assurances to reimburse them.
It is estimated that pediatricians will individually invest nearly 40,000 kroons per month in vaccines, which is a significant amount.
It's going to be far from easy, according to Cabrnochova.
