Conscious authorities as well as the U.S. Interest Section in Havana are trying to have access to the detainee who was arrested on 5 December.
Precinctical charges have not been made public, although under Cuban law, a Cuban citizen or a foreign visitor may be arrested on the pretext of being “dangerous”.
All so-called revolutionary activities, including moderate protests and critical writings, run the risk of an adjunct.
Anti-government graffiti and speeches are seen as serious crimes.
Cuba has an ever-greater blogging community, led by Yoani Sanchez, a popular commentor who often writes about how husband and she is followed and harassed by government officials.
