On the island, the use of the Internet is extremely limited.
It is commercially available in luxurious hotels and foreign-visit visitors to the country, as well as some government buildings, such as universities.
Cubans who often wish to log in must communicate their names to the Government.
Access to many websites is restricted.
The detention of an American in Cuba is rare.
Most of the few Americans incarcerated in Cuba are behind sibling for crimes such as drug trafficking, says Gloria Berbena, press officer at the U.S. Interests Section in Havana.
