The New Silicon-valley
For a long time it had the reputation of a secret city, forbidden to Western visitors.
One of the ten districts of Moscow was, under the Soviet regime, a place for secret armament research under strict surveillance.
Today with its 216,000 inhabitants at 37 km from the center of Moscow, the commune has a reputation as the Soviet Silicon Valley.
Important production and research locations in micro- and nano-electronics are located there.
As early as September 2008, representatives have created links with Riedberg, a venue for the French-French sciences – with the academic institutions and companies of the Frankfurt Innovations Centre.
There were reciprocal meetings, and last Wednesday there have been representatives of Riedberg ratified a “Protocol of close cooperation”.
