Mazda wants to prove that sportsmanship isn’t angry with respect for the environment.
To this end, the Mazda3 newly integrated the engine shut-off and booby-drilling system, dubbed i-Stop, a device which, at least for the time being, is only available on the 150-horsequity 2.0 gasoline engine.
Mazda’s second-strengthened is illustrated by the good score it achieved as a whole.
Detail, vehicle finish, habitability, behaviour, mechanics, i-Stop system...
All of these are remarkable about the new Mazda.
Beginning with the racing desk, it turns out to have excellent ergonomic ergonomics and fasteners.
The touch of the steering wheel is also particularly pleasant.
Continuous the set formed by the control panel and console, we see how Mazda continued in the Japanese tendency to create a futuristic interior design, with many buttons and controls, as well as vivid colors in red and blue.
This style reminds us, in part, that of the Honda Civic.
That is why we can say that both the Mazda3 and Civic, both of Japan, are contrasting with the sobriety of German products, and in particular with the Volkswagen Golf, which everyone wants to surpass.
Continuing with the cabin, this compact Japanese car has a more than sufficient habitability to allow four adults to travel with a high level of comfort.
In addition, there is a great trunk with regular forms.
The automatic engine shut-off and booby-drive system, at least for now, is only available on the gasoline-powered two-litre and 150-horsequity gasoline engine with a manual six-shield change.
This engine is a real bliss. It stands out for its fineness, its low noise, its performance and the control of its consumption.
Indeed, although the most in-demand Mazda3 are diesel models, those that do not run a large number of kilometers per year should not exclude this i-Stop with gasoline engines, both for its high speed comfort and for its controlled consumption.
With regard to the level of equipment, the model chosen for the test is the sportive, i.e. that which has the largest number of serial elements.
Among mass-produced equipment, lane-changing assistant (RVM) that removes blind spots, traction and stability controls, cruise control, photo-resusceptible interior mirror, on-board computer on a large-size screen, parking sensors, independent air-conditioning, rain and light sensor, bluetooth and bluetooth audio, as well as 17-inch alignment wheels.
In addition, as if this equipment were not sufficient, this version had Pack Premium which, for an additional EUR 1,500, includes, inter alia, bi-xon-admovable headlifting headlights and a BOSE audio system with disk loader.
Conclusion
The Mazda3 2.0 i-Stop is one of the best compact cars in its class.
It is illustrated in particular by the quality of the materials used, its behaviour and its high level of equipment.
In addition, those who don't make many kilometers per year will be able to opt for the i-Stop version associated only with 150 husking gasoline 2.0 engine.
The only drawback of this model is its high price, which ranges between EUR 21,770 for the Luxury finish and EUR 23,2270 for the model tested, the Sportive.
In return for this important sum, the Mazda3 will give us a great dose of satisfaction every day.
