Of course, we filed a complaint at the local police station, even though we doubt that this would be very useful and, in order not to affect sensitivities, we just want to make it clear that coarse assassins were Spaniard.
Indigence has led us to denunciate this fact.
We don't understand what's going on among young people so that they find it amusing to mistreat a defence-free animal that gives us gentlism, friendship and keeps us company.
We don't know where proper education and respect for animals and people went.
Michelin and Fesvial, helmet-wearing sets
Tyre manufacturer Michelin, in collaboration with the Espagnole Foundation for Road Safety (Fesvial), has launched a campaign to encourage helmets, mainly among younger motor cyclists, as the two structures have indicated today.
The objective of this initiative is to raise awareness of the importance of wearing helmets, since it is the only element of protection which makes it possible to avoid injuries to the head, or even to death, in the event of a two-wheeled accident.
Michelin stated that this campaign was in line with its commitment to road safety, which “goes beyond the design and manufacture of increasingly reliable products” and has stated that it contributes to this objective through other educational and informative actions.
This new two-White Helmet-Furncated Instruction, under the motto “To be or not to be”, will include a first phase during which posters will be distributed in more than 500 motorcycle garages, in order to guarantee its widest dissemination.
Finally, Michelin pointed out that road safety “is a constant concern” for the company, because, as a tyre manufacturer for two-wheel-drive vehicles, one of its main objectives is to develop increasingly secure products.
Sale of light commercial vehicles is progressing
After almost two years, the market for light commercial vehicles is beginning to see a little bit of light at the end of the tunnel.
The 9,42 425 vehicles registered in Spain in November represent an increase of 12.6% compared to 2008 and, more importantly, they represent the first increase after 22 consecutive months of decline, according to figures from the employers’ trade union Anfac and Ganvam, the dealer.
However, the good tidings must be qualified, since the benchmark for the comparison in the month of November 2008 was particularly bad, compared with a decrease of 60 % compared to the previous year.
As a result, despite last month’s bouncing rebound, the registrations accumulated during these 11-month periods are 40 % less than in the previous financial year.
Since January, by summoning all vehicles that fall into the category of light commercial vehicles (drift-drivers, pick-ups, vans, light vans and light chassis lorries), 95 853 have been sold.
The big clouds that affect their most demands have not dissatisfied, because, although they are also purchased by individuals, most purchases are made by small or medium-sized enterprises, which pay in almost 100 per cent with external financing.
Thus, in addition to the restrictions implied by the limitation of bank loans, other factors must be added, such as an increase in the unemployment rate or the persistence of poor economic economic conditions.
Faced with this situation and the difference between passenger cars, the 2000E purchasing aid has been of little use.
In addition to private individuals, self-beneficiaries and SMEs who wish to acquire a light commercial vehicle of less than EUR 3.5 tonnes with a Co2 emission level which does not more than 160 grams per kilometre may also benefit, but the number of operations speaks for itself.
Yesterday at Ganvam reiterated once again the need for the administration to pay particular attention to these vehicles and also to industrial vehicles (trucks and buses).
Delicators’ association forecasts a similar year in 2010 as it ends, for which it calculates a fall in sales (of passenger and 4x4) of 19%.
Emergency braking aid is now mandatory
As this has taken place with the ABS anti-platform system and as this will take place with ESP stability control, emergency brake support systems will be an obligatory element on European cars.
Moreover, they are already compulsory on newly registered passenger cars and light commercial vehicles, whereas for the rest of the vehicles a waiting period has been set until the end of February 2011.
The measure, imposed by the European Union, aims to tighten the protection of pedestals, even if, through its mode of action, it can also help to avoid many rear-facing shocks.
The Emergency Brake Wage Assistant acts by increasing the pressure on the brakes in the event of an emergency detected by the system thanks to the footstroke given by the driver.
But it doesn’t always maintain the pressure until the end.
According to a study carried out by the car component manufacturer Bosch, one-third of the drivers involved in an accident could not press the brauging before the collision, and half of them did not take advantage of its full strength.
Up to 1,100
The intervention of the aid, again, requires the maximum of the brake system, reducing the distance the car needed to stop.
According to an EU study, if all cars were equipped with such components, up to 1,100 lethal accidents in which pedestrians are involved could be avoided every year.
This reduction would be even more important with the popularisation of so-called Intelligent Emergency Brake Systems: it is calculated that one disaster in four with injuries would be averted.
In this case, the vehicle is equipped with a system which, thanks to a radar or a camera, detects obstacles and warns the driver, in addition to acting lightly on the brakes.
If the driver reacts, it helps it by increasing the pressure on the pedal if this is necessary.
If it does not react, and although the collision is inevitable, the device exerts the maximum effort on the brakes in order to minimise damage.
