Default of EUR 63 million at France Télécom to curb competition
The French Competition Regulator imposed a EUR 63 million on France Télécom for its anti-anti-competitive conduct in the Caribbean region belonging to the country.
According to this institution, the operator has limited competition on fixed and mobile telephony by signing exclusive agreements, tariffs and loyalty programmes to consumers in the margins of regulation.
With this sanction, the former French monopoly and still a state-owned company has been accumulating more than EUR 450 million in fines since 1994, because of the obstacles it places on its competitors.
