Their participation in the Champions league earned 476.4 million in Real Madrid and Barça since its creation.
The Champions League has become a source of income for clubs since its inception in 1992.
Indeed, Real Madrid and F.C.Barcelona won 467.4 million, placing them in the third and fifth place of the clubs that pocketed the most money in this competition.
Manchester United is at the top of the list.
Manchester United is at the top of the list.
Gain the UEFA Champions League not only embodies; it is also one of the main sources of income for big clubs.
In fact, the competition allocated EUR 5,362.5 million to the 105 teams (including 12 Spaniard) that have participated in the event since the creation of the tournament during the 1992-1993 season according to UEFA reports.
Real-Med Madrid and F.C. Barcelona were well served during this distribution.
The white club was the third in the mainland to receive the most money for its participation, and the only one, together with A.C. Milan, won the trophy three times.
The Catalan club, which currently holds the title and last winner of the old European Cup in 1992, is fifth on the list.
At the top of the list are Manchester United and Bayern in Munich, the two teams which, in addition, charged the most for their participation in the last Champions League.
And that, although they lost in front of Barça.
On the other hand, Spain is only the third country, as far as money earned by the Champions League is concerned, although it has won more titles than none (five, while Italy has won four, England three and Germany two).
Breakdown
This apparent paradox is explained by UEFA’s complex money-distribution procedure.
For this year, Michel Platini is chaired by Michel Platini plans to earn 1,090 million through the Champions League.
Of this amount, UEFA will spend EUR 413.1 million on fixed payments: each of the 20 clubs that have participated in the classification matches (including Atlético de Madrid) received EUR 2.1 million.
In addition, those who managed to participate received only 3.8 million to be there, in more than EUR 550 000 for every game.
There is also a bonus in the event of victory (EUR 800,000) and tie (400,000 for each team). Those who arrive in the eighth final receive 3 million each, the eight teams arriving in the quarter-final receive 3.3 million.
The last four teams each will receive EUR 4 million.
And the designer will win 9 million, compared to the 5.2 received by the other finalist.
Thus, under fixed payments, one club will earn at least EUR 7.1 million and not more than EUR 31.2 million.
On the other hand, Barça pocketed EUR 2.5 million for winning the European Super Cup in August.
In addition, there are variable payments, to which 337.8 million are spent.
This money is distributed according to the proportional value of each television market.
The Spanish market is one of the most important, and has four dedicated seats.
The champion of the previous year occupies 40 per cent of the money allocated, 30 per cent for the second, 20 per cent for the third and 10 per cent for the fourth.
The other part will be paid depending on the number of matches played during the current year edition.
